    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d222">

                <pb facs="0284" n="219" xml:id="pg219"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.001 Selassie I/348: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-11-26T15:00:00+00:00">November 26, 1936—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 26—11:52 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>571. Department’s 415, November 23, 2 p.m. I have heard nothing in London about
                    such a visit since my 429, September 11, 2 p.m., and in the circumstances it
                    seemed advisable to confine present inquiries to the Foreign Office which stated
                    that they also have heard nothing.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Repeated to Rome.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
